\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2.6cm]{geometry}

\title{Programme Notes: An Evening with the Bach Circle}
\author{Consort of the Residenz}
\date{October 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section*{About Tonight's Programme}

We open with the Partita No.~2 in D~minor, whose closing Chaconne,
{\sc bwv}~1004, has been called a cathedral in sound. The reading
tonight follows the Neue Bach-Ausgabe text throughout.

The Double Concerto in D~minor, BWV 1043, brings our two leaders
into dialogue over the continuo line. Later we cross the channel
for the ``Hunt'' Quartet, KV 387, dedicated to Haydn and played
here in the Peters urtext.

The second half turns to Haydn himself: the E~flat major Sonata,
{\sc hob}.~XVI:49, in the slow-movement ordering favoured by our
continuo group. We close with Beethoven's bagatelle WoO 80,
``F\"ur Elise'', in the arrangement prepared for the BBC
Philharmonic's 2024 tour.

\section*{Performers}

The Consort of the Residenz plays on period instruments tuned to
A = 415~Hz. Tonight's leaders are E.~Markwardt and J.~Okonkwo,
with continuo realised by the house duo.

\end{document}

